---
// Journey (docs-redesign stage 3 signature 3 rev 2; stage 4 template 5):
// one `vorpal build example` of the Python template, through the CLI and
// config program, the agent daemon and Vorpal.lock, the worker, the local
// store, the registry and a second machine. "What if" switches between a
// first build, building again, editing src/main.py and a second machine.
//
// The scene (SVG, parcels prebuilt), the controls and the text version are
// HTML here, ported once from the stage 4 template. Its title is the
// page's Markdown heading `{#j1-h}` right above it (so "On this page",
// search and the Markdown copy see it), which labels the section. Without JavaScript the
// controls hide and the text version is open; with it, a small inline
// script closes the text version before first paint, and
// src/scripts/journey.js loads when the element nears the viewport or on
// the first interaction (a click on Play that comes first is replayed).
import './journey.css';
---

